WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:02.380
- All right, so Demi,
you've been very vocal

00:00:02.380 --> 00:00:05.790
which I appreciate because
we have gigantic platforms

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:07.179
that I think we should use.

00:00:07.179 --> 00:00:09.910
But you've been pretty vocal
about Black Lives Matter,

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:13.240
so what do you think, personally,

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:16.170
that we can all do differently?

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:19.800
- I think the first step
is educating ourselves.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:21.730
We have a lot of time
on our hands right now.

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:23.750
There's no reason why
we shouldn't be watching

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:26.899
these movies, watching and absorbing

00:00:26.899 --> 00:00:29.040
all information that we possibly can

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:30.750
about what's going on in the world.

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:34.930
And then from there, we've seen it

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:38.600
all over the media that being silent

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:41.500
and being not-racist
is not enough anymore.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:45.103
And that's kind of something
that I posted about.

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:50.660
Like a month ago when the
Ahmaud Arbery stuff happened,

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:54.640
I was like, I felt, I saw online

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:57.770
what had happened and I
felt this overwhelming sense

00:00:57.770 --> 00:01:01.890
of frustration, anger, I was like crying

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:05.083
and I started writing in my phone.

00:01:06.790 --> 00:01:09.280
I just got all my
emotions and I felt guilty

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:12.400
that I hadn't been doing
more and saying more

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:16.920
as an ally but I was also afraid

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:21.693
that people were going to come at me.

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:23.850
- Because they will.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:27.370
- Yeah, so because
everybody's angry right now

00:01:27.370 --> 00:01:29.130
and I just didn't want anyone to think

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:30.490
that I had the wrong intentions.

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:32.680
Or that I was uneducated, you know?

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:34.940
Like, speaking about something

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:37.440
that I didn't know about,
that was a fear of mine.

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:41.133
And so I kind of, when that happened,

00:01:41.990 --> 00:01:45.730
and even before I found
out about George Floyd.

00:01:45.730 --> 00:01:47.587
I was like, "No, I need to do more.

00:01:47.587 --> 00:01:48.737
"I need to be an ally.

00:01:48.737 --> 00:01:49.850
"I have not been an ally."

00:01:49.850 --> 00:01:54.140
I have, like Aretha
Franklin, Billie Holiday,

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:55.900
Whitney Houston, these women of color

00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:59.070
have shaped my musical journey

00:01:59.070 --> 00:02:02.550
and how am I supposed to appreciate

00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:05.760
what they've given me and not stand up

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:07.420
for their community?

00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:11.310
And so I just, I switched my thinking

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:12.960
and then all of this happened.

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:15.390
And you know, I wish I had kinda come

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:17.960
to that realization sooner but I think

00:02:17.960 --> 00:02:20.230
everything happens in it's own timing

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:22.150
and I've gotten to a place where like,

00:02:22.150 --> 00:02:24.527
because I'm able to
deal with my own demons

00:02:24.527 --> 00:02:28.090
and my own things, I can now kind of help

00:02:28.090 --> 00:02:29.500
advocate for other people.

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:30.950
And I think maybe that's a reason

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:33.340
why some people aren't
speaking out and doing things,

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:34.850
is they're afraid but they're also

00:02:34.850 --> 00:02:36.563
not ready to help other people.

00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:40.170
I don't know, I just wanted to be

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:42.500
the ally that I know I can be

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:45.510
and I want to be able
to share the thinking

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:47.970
as much as possible because the legacy

00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:49.250
that I will leave as a person

00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:51.010
will last so much longer than the music

00:02:51.010 --> 00:02:52.440
that we leave behind.

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:54.770
- Yeah, totally, your
character means everything.

00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:55.603
I agree.

